Operator: 'decode tn36's property-change codes and solve L5.' DONE.

PROPERTY CODES DECODED (codes 14/15/63 = htntnzkbzu.knfgrcbayu(arg), set the
sjmtdfxdrc property ABSOLUTELY): probed by directly invoking each command on a
fresh L5 env -> code 14->9, code 15->8, code 63->15. Added PROP_CODE map
{9:14, 8:15, 15:63} to compute_moves; code 63 = all 6 bit-buttons set.

L5 SOLVED: obj (49,8,scale1,rot270,prop11) -> tgt (49,20,scale2,rot0,prop15) needs
3 downs + scale-up(8) + rotate90(5) + property->15(63) -- the first level needing
ALL transform classes at once. The ordering search interleaves them correctly.
Reproduces L1-L5 (reproduced=True claimed_level=5, 53 clicks). Registry: tn36
levels_reproduced 4->5, reproducible_total 19->20.

L6 frontier: position program [33,33,33,33,33,2] computes but no ordering wins ->
another obstacle/routing wrinkle (tighter gap or a 7th move). Logged.
